1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,821
Question seventeen. Highlight: “sixteen-bit” colour depth; how many colours can be represented?

2
00:00:06,821 --> 00:00:11,632
Useful: count = two to the power of bit depth = two to the sixteen.

3
00:00:11,632 --> 00:00:15,222
Useless: camera brand — does not change the maths.

4
00:00:15,222 --> 00:00:19,387
Option A. Sixteen: mistaking depth for colour count — cut.

5
00:00:19,387 --> 00:00:25,275
Option B. Sixty-five thousand five hundred thirty-six = two to the sixteen — keep.

6
00:00:25,275 --> 00:00:31,235
Option C. Thirty-two thousand seven hundred sixty-eight = two to the fifteen — cut.

7
00:00:31,235 --> 00:00:35,327
Option D. Two hundred fifty-six = two to the eight — cut.

8
00:00:35,327 --> 00:00:41,431
Sixteen-bit depth → two to the sixteen = sixty-five thousand five hundred thirty-six.

9
00:00:41,431 --> 00:00:43,872
Therefore the correct answer is B.

